    <div class="header-actions"><details class="site-menu"><summary>Menu</summary><div class="site-menu-panel"><p>AVOCADOMINI R5</p><nav aria-label="Product navigation"><a href="#experience"><strong>Experience</strong></a><a href="#design"><strong>Design</strong></a><a href="/create/"><strong>Create games</strong></a><a href="#status"><strong>Development</strong></a><a href="/install/"><strong>RockstarOS</strong></a><a href="https://avocadopro.si/"><strong>avocadoPro</strong></a></nav></div></details><a class="header-cta" href="/preorder/">Price & status <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="r5-hero" aria-labelledby="r5-title">
      <div class="r5-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">AVOCADOMINI R5 / PRODUCT VISION</p><h1 id="r5-title">One device.<br /><em>More ways to live.</em></h1><p class="lead">A spatial companion for home, play, work, and the moments you take with you.</p><div class="r5-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#experience">Explore the idea <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#status">See what is real today ↗</a></div><p class="hero-truth"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Design and feasibility stage · No physical R5 accepted · No sales</p></div>
      <figure class="r5-hero-media"><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-slim-home-concept.png" alt="Concept of a slim silver avocadoMini with a black sensor band and low dock beside a spatial call card" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>Concept visualization. The device, call, and floating display have not been built or validated.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="r5-intro" aria-labelledby="r5-intro-title"><p class="eyebrow">ONE MINI / MANY INTENTIONS</p><h2 id="r5-intro-title">Start with what<br />you want to do.</h2><p>R5 is being designed around one self-contained, detachable unit. Start a call, create without standing at a PC, play, or carry your connection and work with you. Another Mini could stay in a room or under an eave, but the unit you take must still work on its own. Each purpose needs real hardware, service, and permission acceptance before it is available.</p><div class="r5-fact-row"><span>ONE WORKING UNIT FIRST</span><span>≤ 200 MM DESIGN TARGET</span><span>OTHER MINIS OPTIONAL</span></div></section>
    <section class="r5-form" aria-labelledby="r5-form-title"><figure><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-slim-form-reference.png" alt="Design reference showing a slim silver cylindrical Mini with a black sensor band standing on a low round dock" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Product-form reference, not final hardware or a measured production design.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">THE SHAPE WE ARE DESIGNING TOWARD</p><h2 id="r5-form-title">Quiet in a room.<br />Clear in your hand.</h2><p>A slender silver body, one dark sensor band, and a low dock are the visual direction. The cylinder should sit naturally in furniture or a reachable wall dock, then come away without taking its identity and work away from you.</p><p class="r5-form-note">Its final diameter, battery, optics, radio, mass, and manufacture remain unresolved.</p></div></section>
    <section id="experience" class="r5-experience" aria-labelledby="r5-experience-title"><div class="r5-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE EXPERIENCE WE ARE TESTING</p><h2 id="r5-experience-title">A useful day,<br />not a fixed mode.</h2></div><div class="r5-experience-grid"><article><span>01 / LIVE</span><h3>Feel at home.</h3><p>Explore approved room actions and clear, reversible choices. Compatible devices and permissions must be confirmed first.</p></article><article><span>02 / MAKE</span><h3>Keep creating.</h3><p>Start an idea, review an Agent result, and keep the same work and its history as you move.</p></article><article><span>03 / PLAY</span><h3>Move into play.</h3><p>Use spatial input with a supported game. Game availability, sensing quality, and local performance need separate acceptance.</p></article><article><span>04 / CARRY</span><h3>Take it with you.</h3><p>Detach the unit and continue the essentials. Optional domestic LTE/IoT data SIM connectivity, portable power, and calls remain unproven goals.</p></article></div><p class="r5-experience-note">These are intended experiences, not features available on production hardware today.</p></section>
    <section class="r5-create-cta" aria-labelledby="r5-create-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">TAKE PART IN THE BUILD</p><h2 id="r5-create-title">Your next game<br />starts here.</h2><p>Try a browser game starter, make your own version, or send a product idea. The creator preview is open now; Mini hardware and game publication still require separate acceptance.</p></div><a class="button" href="/create/">Create games & send ideas ↗</a></section>
    <section id="design" class="r5-design" aria-labelledby="r5-design-title"><figure><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-removable-dock-concept.png" alt="Concept showing a slim Mini being lifted from a reachable wall dock that stays in place" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Detachable dock concept. Portable power, calls, optional LTE/IoT data SIM service, and Wi-Fi sharing have not been demonstrated.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM HOME TO HAND</p><h2 id="r5-design-title">Leave the dock.<br />Keep your work.</h2><p>Lift one Mini from a reachable wall or furniture dock; the dock stays put. Other installed Minis may remain at home as separate units. The one you carry still needs its own accepted power, identity, connection, and saved job. A ceiling or eave unit is a placement concept, not the everyday dock you must reach to leave.</p><a class="text-link" href="#status">Read the development status ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="r5-vision" aria-labelledby="r5-vision-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE LONGER VIEW</p><h2 id="r5-vision-title">Less screen.<br />More presence.</h2><p>Spatial call notices and hand input are part of the R5 design goal. A sensor alone cannot create a visible image or complete a phone call. Display optics, privacy, recognition, audio, a real network, and fallback controls must work together in one accepted device.</p></div><div class="r5-vision-panel"><span>WHAT MUST BE PROVEN</span><ul><li>Readable and safe spatial output</li><li>Reliable input and owner verification</li><li>Real calls and portable connectivity</li><li>RockstarOS, Sky, and Zema continuity</li></ul></div></section>
    <section id="status" class="r5-status" aria-labelledby="r5-status-title"><div class="r5-status-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CURRENT PRODUCT STATUS / 21 OCT 2026</p><h2 id="r5-status-title">A concept with<br />clear next steps.</h2><p>R5 requirements and experience are documented. No complete Mini prototype has passed the physical acceptance gates.</p></div><div class="r5-status-grid"><article><span>DESIGN</span><strong>In progress</strong><p>One-unit architecture, intended experience, and acceptance gates are written.</p></article><article><span>PHYSICAL DEVICE</span><strong>Not accepted</strong><p>Display, sensing, calls, optional LTE connectivity, power, heat, and recovery have not passed together.</p></article><article><span>ROCKSTAROS ON MINI</span><strong>Not available</strong><p>No signed, recoverable Mini OS image or public Mini installer has been accepted.</p></article><article><span>SALES</span><strong>Closed</strong><p>No reservation, payment, final R5 price, or release date is available.</p></article></div><div class="r5-status-actions"><a class="button" href="/preorder/">Full status & next steps ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/install/">Available Web preview & OS status ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="r5-ecosystem" aria-labelledby="r5-ecosystem-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">CONNECTED BY DESIGN</p><h2 id="r5-ecosystem-title">One foundation.<br />Different hardware.</h2><p>RockstarOS provides the device runtime; Sky connects Agents and tools; Zema tracks work, approval, results, and spending. avocadoPro is a separate AI-dedicated PC. Mini should stand on its own first, with supported pairing as an option.</p></div><div class="r5-ecosystem-links"><a href="https://avoado.si/">Explore the avokado service <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://avocadopro.si/">Explore avocadoPro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/install/">Check RockstarOS access <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
